questions.answer:
You can start by looking over the courses in the course catalogue (
https://www.mcgill.ca/study/2022-2023/courses/search
). I wrote down the ones I found interesting, and waited for the minerva registration portal to open around a month before the semester started. Then I started registering, but many courses were already filled because the exchange students are let in on the site later. However, people add/drop until 2 weeks into the semester, so if you check minerva regularly (a couple of times a day), you will most likely be able to get the courses you want.
